Subject: [PATCH] prompts: instruct informative log narration in interactive
 and batch compute
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Every submitted job must narrate itself in its logs: a startup banner
(phase, run identity, output destination), bounded progress lines during
long stages, one line per phase transition, an exit summary naming
results and artifact paths, errors logged with the context that produced
them, and unbuffered output. Interactive srun / run_in_on_demand_session
commands follow the same rule at command scale: print what the command
checks and end with a named result line.

The rule is owned by the compute_execution fragment (per the
one-authoritative-statement convention); the line-level recipe lives in
the /slurm skill's new 'Log narration' section; the live interactive-mode
block gains one reinforcing sentence in its shared tail (rendered by both
the Slurm and on-demand arms).

Context: #public-silico-feedback 2026-08-14 — 'we should probably
instruct Silico to give more informative logs', and the follow-up that
interactive worker sessions are the least visible surface.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Kx9FKL3kuASgoaWy6XoN8u
